<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">27 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 27 July, from 1214 to 2012.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-france" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-france.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1214">1214 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">812 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Philip II of France wins the Battle of Bouvines</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-france">Philip Augustus</a> defeated Emperor Otto IV and his allies, backed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, at Bouvines. The defeat wrecked John's hopes of recovering Normandy and weakened him before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magna-carta">Magna Carta</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1694">1694 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">332 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Bank of England receives its royal charter</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bank-of-england">Bank of England</a> was founded to lend 1.2 million pounds to William III's government for war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. It became the model for central banks around the world.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bank-of-england">Bank of England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1953">1953 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">73 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Armistice ends the fighting in the Korean War</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-11-november-1918">armistice</a> signed at Panmunjom halted three years of war that had cost millions of lives. It created a demilitarised zone roughly along the 38th parallel, but no peace treaty has ever been signed.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1996">1996 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">30 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bomb explodes in Atlanta's Centennial Olympic Park</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A pipe bomb exploded during a concert at the Atlanta Olympics, killing one woman and injuring 111. Security guard Richard Jewell was wrongly suspected; Eric Rudolph later confessed.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2012">2012 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">14 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Danny Boyle's ceremony opens the London Olympics</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> 2012 Olympics opened with 'Isles of Wonder', a ceremony tracing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> from rural idyll through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/industrial-revolution">Industrial Revolution</a> to the NHS and pop culture. It was watched by hundreds of millions.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/industrial-revolution">Industrial Revolution</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li></ol>
